{
  "info": {
    "name": "Mini Operations ERP",
    "description": "Full API for the Mini Operations ERP.\n\n## Getting started\n1. Set `baseUrl` if the API is not on http://localhost:3000/api.\n2. Run the three requests in **0 \u00b7 Auth** \u2014 each stores its token in a collection variable, so nothing else needs manual copying.\n3. Run **1 \u00b7 Bootstrap IDs** to capture location, item, batch and user ids.\n4. Everything after that is ready to send.\n\n## The interesting requests\n- *Sales tries to create a work order* \u2192 403 (mandatory test 5)\n- *Dispatch transfer* then *Inventory at destination* \u2192 unchanged (mandatory test 3)\n- *Receive transfer* twice \u2192 409 (mandatory test 4)\n- *Reserve order* beyond availability \u2192 409 (mandatory test 1)\n- *Reconcile* \u2192 proves the ledger still balances",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:3000/api"
    },
    {
      "key": "password",
      "value": "Password@123"
    },
    {
      "key": "adminToken",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "opsToken",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "salesToken",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "locationA",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "locationB",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "itemId",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "batchId",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "opsUserId",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "inventoryId",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "workOrderId",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "transferId",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "orderId",
      "value": ""
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "0 \u00b7 Auth",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Login as Admin",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/login",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "auth",
                "login"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Signs in and stores the token in the `adminToken` collection variable.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"admin@ops-erp.local\",\n  \"password\": \"{{password}}\"\n}"
            }
          },
          "response": [],
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('adminToken', body.accessToken);",
                  "console.log('Signed in as', body.user.role);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
